message: "If you use this framework, skills, or methodology in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ABMforAI: Rigorous, Evidence-Based Agent-Based Modeling Guidelines and Skills for AI Assistants"
authors:
  - name: "ABMforAI Contributors"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Unevem/ABMforAI"
url: "https://github.com/Unevem/ABMforAI"
keywords:
  - "agent-based-modeling"
  - "computational-social-science"
  - "artificial-intelligence"
  - "odd-protocol"
  - "mesa-framework"
  - "reproducibility"
  - "simulation"
  - "evidence-gated"
abstract: >-
  ABMforAI is an open-source framework, agent skill suite, and methodological guideline
  designed to empower domain researchers to design, document (ODD Protocol),
  implement (Python/Mesa 3.5+), and verify computational simulations with AI assistants
  while eliminating theoretical hallucinations and undocumented behavioral assumptions.
